//@ compile-fail
//@ requires: madaros
//@ error-pattern: algebra declares a reassociation strategy its multiplication law cannot certify
//
// Axis 1 of anti-garbling at the declaration (formal/lean4/EpistemicEffectsNSA.lean,
// `assocCert`, `reassoc_sound`, witness W1). `reassociate: free` is a claim that the
// compiler may re-order products at will. On an alternative (non-associative) product the
// claim is false: for e1, e2, e4 the two parenthesizations differ by 2·e7
// (`w1_reassoc_changes_value`) and the sensitivity of the product changes too
// (`w1_sensitivity_changes`). Granting it is an order-fabrication licence — E252.
//
// Measured 2026-09-01 on the committed Madaros (md5 ff69dae4): `check: OK`.

algebra Octonion over f64 {
    add: commutative, associative
    mul: alternative, non_commutative
    reassociate: free
}

fn main() -> i64 with IO { 0 }
